==Finnish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fi|urj-fin-pro|*kumpu}}, probably from {{inh|fi|urj-pro|*kumpa||wave}}, whence also {{cog|myv|кумбо||burdock}}, {{cog|mdf|комба||hump}} and {{cog|hu|hab||foam}}. Contains a {{m|fi|-u}} suffix which is not seen in the earlier derivation {{m|fi|kumpare}}. The Finnic root has also been compared with {{ncog|gem-pro|*humpaz}} (whence {{ncog|en|hump}}), possibly hinting that it is borrowed from Germanic instead.

